\section*{1. Executive Summary & Review Objective}
This protocol outlines the validation framework for testing the \textbf{Astrophysical Telemetry Encryption \& Anomaly Detection Module (ATEDM)}. The primary objective of the upcoming peer review is twofold: 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Independently run the custom FPGA pipeline logic against publicly archived James Webb Space Telescope (JWST) deep field raw telemetry to verify baseline object classification and astrometric catalog matching.
    \item Evaluate the anomaly detection engine's high-$\sigma$ flagging thresholds against known transient populations to isolate novel, unclassified signals under strict hardware-enforced constraints.
\end{enumerate}

\section*{2. System Architecture & Pipeline Specifications}
The architecture circumvents traditional commercial computing bottlenecks via dedicated hardware acceleration:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Sensor-Interface FPGA Ingestion:} Custom synthesizable SystemVerilog RTL deployed on Xilinx/AMD UltraScale+ nodes executes inline pixel decoding, background subtraction, and parity checking with $<5\text{ ns}$ latency.
    \item \textbf{High-Capacity Shared Memory Buffers:} Multi-channel DDR4/DDR5 memory banks integrated directly into the sensor housing absorb multi-gigabit data surges, preventing frame-drop anomalies during peak cadence.
    \item \textbf{Post-Quantum Cryptographic Wrapper:} Every telemetry frame is secured at wire speed using hardware-accelerated \texttt{ML-KEM-1024} key encapsulation and \texttt{ML-DSA-87} digital signatures prior to non-secure bus transmission.
    \item \textbf{Thermal Envelope:} Continuous operation at a sustained 1,000 W thermal design power (TDP) is governed by custom dual-sided vapor chamber manifolds.
\end{itemize}

\section*{3. Independent Verification Protocol for Reviewers}
To establish empirical performance parity and validation, participating independent astrophysicists will execute the following sequence:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Dataset Ingestion Phase:} Ingest raw, uncalibrated FITS files from public JWST NIRCam and NIRSpec deep field repositories.
    \item \textbf{Baseline Cross-Checking:} Process data through the ATEDM pipeline to verify that standard galaxies, known variable stars, and cataloged transients are tagged with identical positional and photometric accuracy compared to standard pipeline reductions.
    \item \textbf{Anomaly Isolation Test:} Isolate outlier signals exceeding user-defined $\sigma$ thresholds. Compare signal-to-noise ratios, morphological sorting, and multi-spectral signature curves against standard anomaly registries.
\end{enumerate}

